{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01L7KbEkDx4V7pgb2xKhFw23","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"a0bda4fd-a29f-4ebe-b5da-0249a6d1079d","ownerOrganizationUuid":"d338ef42-a650-40c7-a017-e1dca5ad4850"}
{"parentUuid":"4ed954df-2379-4380-8290-f03d1b5c52b0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01DF4BpkG5tP657K7U5vC3Qm","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"51c8988b-edf1-467d-a233-31b86b0e6914","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:14:15.236Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
{"parentUuid":"51c8988b-edf1-467d-a233-31b86b0e6914","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEjSDu7cCqrzCtCzV1rH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 11 CodeQL alerts are closed. The 7 cyclic-import alerts closed when CodeQL scanned `main` after #2510 merged. My #2510 then left one dead variable behind, which CodeQL flagged as #217; PR #2513 removes it.\n\n**Open standards are now a written, checked requirement (PR #2512, new rule 45)**\n\n| Standard | Where it applies | How it's enforced |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenAPI | Every REST operation | New contract test: every operation needs a summary and a typed success response. The spec and client are regenerated in the PR, and CI's drift checks compare them. |\n| OpenTelemetry | Traces, logs and metrics | Telemetry goes out only through the OTel SDK seam, and no proprietary APM SDK may be added. A new boundary test enforces this. |\n| OpenLineage | Lineage events | Same boundary test. Lineage events are built only in the lineage package. |\n| ODCS v3 | Data contracts (#1977, Week 5) | DataQ-specific fields go in ODCS custom properties, never a parallel format. I noted this on #1977. |\n| OIDC, SPDX, Vault KV v2, API compatibility policy | Sign-in, SBOM, secret store, versioning | Named in the rule; the existing gates already cover them. |\n\nThe new boundary checks pass on today's code, and each fails when I add a stray import. Rule 44, which requires new code to meet the existing standards including a11y, is in the same PR. The PR template's checklist covers both rules.\n\n**Enforcing the OpenAPI rule turned up a live bug (#2514, fixed by PR #2515).** The comparison-report download serves CSV or XLSX files, but the published spec documented it as JSON. The generated `dataq-client` therefore crashed on every real download. #2515 declares the real file types and makes the client return the file's bytes. It also adds the contract test, which fails without the fix. It was the only one of the 170 operations missing a typed response.\n\n**Merge order:** #2513 and #2515 first, then #2512, because rule 45 names #2515's test. All three PRs are waiting on CI.\n\n**Still running:** the rule-44 audit of the UI v1.3 has shipped so far.\n\n**Still open:** Dependabot #50 and #51. The fix is on `main`; I'll check them again once GitHub's dependency graph refreshes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1170,"cache_read_input_tokens":647583,"output_tokens":801,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1170,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":801,"cache_read_input_tokens":647583,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1170,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1170},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5d91ffe8-36dd-49f7-ba24-c03311c143ed","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEjSDWoY7ucyYcbQ2CYR","requestRef":"25aaf2c4-c730-4dcb-8441-eb72c711e805","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"65429f67-5e39-442d-97f8-abfc4dc55c44","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:14:15.235Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
