{"parentUuid":"42d66de5-6d53-4ed6-ab25-ce06aa217f25","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7ac3f933-5091-4252-a265-5d5d96c713cb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_0175DeBAgpYTLxjikzr9AQAM","content":"Skill \"code-review\" completed (forked execution).\n\nResult:\nI found no correctness problems in PR #2513. It deletes 2 lines from `backend/app/datasources/flatfile.py`: the `_FILE_TYPES = FLAT_FILE_TYPES` alias and the `FLAT_FILE_TYPES` import it used. I searched backend, packages, scripts, frontend and docs (tests included) on the PR branch and found no remaining use of either. The code after the deletion is also still valid Python formatting.\n\nThere are two optional cleanups in files the PR doesn't touch, so the 5-finding floor wasn't met. I posted a summary as a regular PR comment rather than inline comments, because neither cleanup sits on a line in the diff: https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2513#issuecomment-6308284249\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"backend/app/services/schema_drift.py\",\n    \"line\": 49,\n    \"summary\": \"Same private-alias pattern this PR removes: `_FILE_TYPES = FLAT_FILE_TYPES`, used once at line 228.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"No runtime bug. It's an extra layer of indirection with no purpose, and if line 228 ever moves to `FLAT_FILE_TYPES` the alias becomes dead and CodeQL flags `py/unused-global-variable` again (the same class as alert 217). Inline `FLAT_FILE_TYPES` and delete the alias.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"backend/app/services/check_service.py\",\n    \"line\": 113,\n    \"summary\": \"`SCHEMA_DRIFT_CAPABLE_TYPES` adds `*FILE_TYPES` again, but `MONITOR_CAPABLE_TYPES` (line 109) already contains it.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Harmless no-op, but misleading: a reader assumes the schema-drift set covers more types than the monitor set because of the file types, when the two are identical. Drop the redundant `*FILE_TYPES`.\"\n  }\n]\n```"}]},"uuid":"0edaead8-fe3e-46fb-8cc3-2b0531d589e9","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:47:23.830Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"commandName":"code-review","status":"forked","agentId":"a684fdb1d9811e36d","result":"I found no correctness problems in PR #2513. It deletes 2 lines from `backend/app/datasources/flatfile.py`: the `_FILE_TYPES = FLAT_FILE_TYPES` alias and the `FLAT_FILE_TYPES` import it used. I searched backend, packages, scripts, frontend and docs (tests included) on the PR branch and found no remaining use of either. The code after the deletion is also still valid Python formatting.\n\nThere are two optional cleanups in files the PR doesn't touch, so the 5-finding floor wasn't met. I posted a summary as a regular PR comment rather than inline comments, because neither cleanup sits on a line in the diff: https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2513#issuecomment-6308284249\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"backend/app/services/schema_drift.py\",\n    \"line\": 49,\n    \"summary\": \"Same private-alias pattern this PR removes: `_FILE_TYPES = FLAT_FILE_TYPES`, used once at line 228.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"No runtime bug. It's an extra layer of indirection with no purpose, and if line 228 ever moves to `FLAT_FILE_TYPES` the alias becomes dead and CodeQL flags `py/unused-global-variable` again (the same class as alert 217). Inline `FLAT_FILE_TYPES` and delete the alias.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"backend/app/services/check_service.py\",\n    \"line\": 113,\n    \"summary\": \"`SCHEMA_DRIFT_CAPABLE_TYPES` adds `*FILE_TYPES` again, but `MONITOR_CAPABLE_TYPES` (line 109) already contains it.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Harmless no-op, but misleading: a reader assumes the schema-drift set covers more types than the monitor set because of the file types, when the two are identical. Drop the redundant `*FILE_TYPES`.\"\n  }\n]\n```"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8702ab19-308b-4ddf-a51c-a7544c8a7269","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Codin