{"parentUuid":"8345ca50-c18a-45f1-b099-c86496d53d8a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEpMVdsLFX3TXmmvD4TL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F9bvummrKUzHkCHPTX93CY","name":"Skill","input":{"skill":"code-review","args":"2515 --comment medium"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":537,"cache_read_input_tokens":656492,"output_tokens":131,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":28},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":537,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":131,"cache_read_input_tokens":656492,"cache_creation_input_tokens":537,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":537},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01F9bvummrKUzHkCHPTX93CY":{"skill":"code-review","args":"2515 --comment medium"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d53bf23e-c941-482a-b037-b1ac0428cc66","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgEpMUYcxmj3WhWRwJx29","requestRef":"3a4472f4-0fd7-47fe-ab0d-0fd565a58906","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ef88fd3a-ba68-4bed-9e49-c31e30f4dbc1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:18:59.651Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
{"parentUuid":"ef88fd3a-ba68-4bed-9e49-c31e30f4dbc1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"429dd6a2-e50c-4f9b-bdde-be5a4b9a7a7c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_01F9bvummrKUzHkCHPTX93CY","content":"Skill \"code-review\" completed (forked execution).\n\nResult:\nI reviewed PR #2515 at high effort and posted all 7 findings as inline comments on the PR. None of the findings are crashes. The worst is that the new contract test would still pass on the exact bug class it was written to stop. These comments open review threads, and unresolved threads block merging into `main`, so each one needs resolving before the PR can merge.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\",\"line\":30,\"summary\":\"The typed-success check accepts any non-empty schema, so it does not catch the client-breaking shape this PR fixes: a non-JSON media type missing from openapi-config.yaml's content_type_overrides.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"A new route declares text/plain or application/pdf with {\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\"} (the same shape as this PR's own fixture at L59). The test passes, and the generated client returns response.text or builds BytesIO(str), which raises. Nothing fails until a user downloads the file.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/app/api/v1/runs.py\",\"line\":676,\"summary\":\"Only the 200 is declared. The handler's 404 is missing from the spec, and its 422 is typed as HTTPValidationError although the app returns the {\\\"error\\\":{...}} envelope.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"An unknown run_id gives a 404, so sync() returns None (with raise_on_unexpected_status False) and gives no reason. A non-comparison result gives a 422, and HTTPValidationError.from_dict pops the missing 'detail' key, so the client gets an empty object and the message is lost. The 422 mismatch affects every operation in the spec.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/app/api/v1/runs.py\",\"line\":681,\"summary\":\"The CSV/XLSX media types are hand-copied from comparison_report.build_report, and a third time into openapi-config.yaml.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"If a format is added to REPORT_FORMATS or a media type changes in build_report, the spec and client keep describing the old set and no test fails.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\",\"line\":23,\"summary\":\"_typed_success passes an operation as soon as any one 2xx is typed (or a literal '204' is present).\",\"failure_scenario\":\"An operation with a typed 201 and an untyped 200 {\\\"application/json\\\":{\\\"schema\\\":{}}} passes the gate, and the generated client parses that 200 as Any.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\",\"line\":30,\"summary\":\"The check `media.get('schema')` is a truthiness test, so a schema that holds only a title counts as typed.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"A schema such as {\\\"title\\\":\\\"Response Foo\\\"} (a shape FastAPI can emit for an Any-annotated return) passes even though it constrains nothing. Nothing in today's spec has this shape, so the gap is latent.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\",\"line\":44,\"summary\":\"test_every_operation_has_a_summary duplicates the existing test_main.py::test_every_api_endpoint_has_summary_and_tags.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"Two near-identical summary guardrails, each with its own method-walk loop, are maintained separately and differ only in whether /healthz is in scope. A fix to one will not reach the other.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"packages/dataq-client/src/dataq_client/generated/api/runs/download_comparison_report.py\",\"line\":44,\"summary\":\"The client returns File(payload=BytesIO(...)) with no file_name or mime_type, and the changelog says it returns 'bytes'.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"A sync() caller cannot tell CSV from XLSX or recover comparison-<id>.<fmt> without dropping down to sync_detailed().headers. The changelog fragment misdescribes the return type.\"}\n]\n```\n\nThe client fix itself is correct: the 200 response is now parsed as a file rather than JSON. The suite YAML export, which looked like the same class of bug, is already handled by the hand-written `export_suite_yaml` method in `/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/packages/dataq-client/src/dataq_client/client.py`.\n\nThe second finding covers a problem broader than this PR: every 422 in the spec is typed as `HTTPValidationError`, but `_validation_exception_handler` in `/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/backend/app/core/errors.py` returns the DataQ error envelope. Under the repo's \"fixed or filed\" rule it needs its own issue if this PR doesn't fix it."}]},"uuid":"27b94c13-4665-4da5-b266-1bb3708eeaf3","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:21:43.402Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"commandName":"code-review","status":"forked","agentId":"a7263dae4522a23a6","result":"I reviewed PR #2515 at high effort and posted all 7 findings as inline comments on the PR. None of the findings are crashes. The worst is that the new contract test would still pass on the exact bug class it was written to stop. These comments open review threads, and unresolved threads block merging into `main`, so each one needs resolving before the PR can merge.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\",\"line\":30,\"summary\":\"The typed-success check accepts any non-empty schema, so it does not catch the client-breaking shape this PR fixes: a non-JSON media type missing from openapi-config.yaml's content_type_overrides.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"A new route declares text/plain or application/pdf with {\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\"} (the same shape as this PR's own fixture at L59). The test passes, and the generated client returns response.text or builds BytesIO(str), which raises. Nothing fails until a user downloads the file.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/app/api/v1/runs.py\",\"line\":676,\"summary\":\"Only the 200 is declared. The handler's 404 is missing from the spec, and its 422 is typed as HTTPValidationError although the app returns the {\\\"error\\\":{...}} envelope.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"An unknown run_id gives a 404, so sync() returns None (with raise_on_unexpected_status False) and gives no reason. A non-comparison result gives a 422, and HTTPValidationError.from_dict pops the missing 'detail' key, so the client gets an empty object and the message is lost. The 422 mismatch affects every operation in the spec.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/app/api/v1/runs.py\",\"line\":681,\"summary\":\"The CSV/XLSX media types are hand-copied from comparison_report.build_report, and a third time into openapi-config.yaml.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"If a format is added to REPORT_FORMATS or a media type changes in build_report, the spec and client keep describing the old set and no test fails.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\",\"line\":23,\"summary\":\"_typed_success passes an operation as soon as any one 2xx is typed (or a literal '204' is present).\",\"failure_scenario\":\"An operation with a typed 201 and an untyped 200 {\\\"application/json\\\":{\\\"schema\\\":{}}} passes the gate, and the generated client parses that 200 as Any.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\",\"line\":30,\"summary\":\"The check `media.get('schema')` is a truthiness test, so a schema that holds only a title counts as typed.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"A schema such as {\\\"title\\\":\\\"Response Foo\\\"} (a shape FastAPI can emit for an Any-annotated return) passes even though it constrains nothing. Nothing in today's spec has this shape, so the gap is latent.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\",\"line\":44,\"summary\":\"test_every_operation_has_a_summary duplicates the existing test_main.py::test_every_api_endpoint_has_summary_and_tags.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"Two near-identical summary guardrails, each with its own method-walk loop, are maintained separately and differ only in whether /healthz is in scope. A fix to one will not reach the other.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"packages/dataq-client/src/dataq_client/generated/api/runs/download_comparison_report.py\",\"line\":44,\"summary\":\"The client returns File(payload=BytesIO(...)) with no file_name or mime_type, and the changelog says it returns 'bytes'.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"A sync() caller cannot tell CSV from XLSX or recover comparison-<id>.<fmt> without dropping down to sync_detailed().headers. The changelog fragment misdescribes the return type.\"}\n]\n```\n\nThe client fix itself is correct: the 200 response is now parsed as a file rather than JSON. The suite YAML export, which looked like the same class of bug, is already handled by the hand-written `export_suite_yaml` method in `/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/packages/dataq-client/src/dataq_client/client.py`.\n\nThe second finding covers a problem broader than this PR: every 422 in the spec is typed as `HTTPValidationError`, but `_validation_exception_handler` in `/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/backend/app/core/errors.py` returns the DataQ error envelope. Under the repo's \"fixed or filed\" rule it needs its own issue if this PR doesn't fix it."},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d53bf23e-c941-482a-b037-b1ac0428cc66","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","root":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ef88fd3a-ba68-4bed-9e49-c31e30f4dbc1","permissionDecision":{"decisio