{"parentUuid":"88607cbe-9b5f-418d-b644-741637c3f2ee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEpmdz5Ryk2proBNuP29","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both halves of the fix are now caught. Regenerating artifacts, fixing the changelog wording, and filing the two deferred findings."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":892,"cache_read_input_tokens":669551,"output_tokens":1642,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":85},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":892,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1642,"cache_read_input_tokens":669551,"cache_creation_input_tokens":892,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":892},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f3f6b978-a86e-4b88-b4fe-4fd6f97923f0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEpmdAU4eRdafrxE7naG","requestRef":"d5037789-c13b-44a5-90db-d0543a718f5f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d9cbd0eb-6575-4ab1-8136-5cf2eea7d50c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:24:06.332Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
{"parentUuid":"d9cbd0eb-6575-4ab1-8136-5cf2eea7d50c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEpmdz5Ryk2proBNuP29","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D1SHQVV9fMRaAsJsZ2NqZ5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"/bin/bash -c 'u=$(grep \"^POSTGRES_USER=\" .env | cut -d= -f2); p=$(grep \"^POSTGRES_PASSWORD=\"REDACTED\"REDACTED\"; $B/python -m backend.scripts.export_docs_reference >/dev/null 2>&1; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-arijit-Coding-Python-DataQ/641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d/scratchpad/ruff0165; PATH=\"$S/bin:$PATH\" $B/python scripts/generate-dataq-client.py >/dev/null 2>&1; PATH=\"$S/bin:$PATH\" $B/python scripts/generate-dataq-client.py --check >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"client rc=$?\"; $B/python -m backend.scripts.export_docs_reference --check >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"export rc=$?\"; $B/python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov backend/tests -k \"comparison or openapi or test_main\" 2>&1 | tail -1'; printf '%s\\n' \"**The comparison-report download is described correctly in the API reference.** It was documented as returning JSON, so the generated Python client failed on every download; the reference now lists its CSV and XLSX media types and the client returns the downloaded file.\" > changelog.d/2514.fixed.md; I1=$(gh issue create --title \"OpenAPI: no operation declares its error responses, and every 422 is typed as FastAPI's HTTPValidationError instead of the DataQ error envelope\" --label \"bug,priority/P2\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 7 — polish: MCP & API, performance, accessibility\" --body \"Found reviewing #2515. None of the 170 operations in \\`docs/site/reference/openapi.json\\` declares a 4xx response other than the auto-added 422, and that 422 is typed as \\`HTTPValidationError\\` while \\`core/errors.py\\`'s handlers return \\`{\\\"error\\\": {\\\"code\\\", \\\"message\\\", \\\"detail\\\"}}\\` (\\`ErrorResponse\\`).\n\nEffect on the generated \\`dataq-client\\`: a 404/403/409 parses to \\`None\\` (or raises only with \\`raise_on_unexpected_status\\`), and a 422 is parsed by \\`HTTPValidationError.from_dict\\`, which finds no \\`detail\\` key and returns an empty object, so the server's message is lost.\n\nFix: register \\`ErrorResponse\\` as the response model for the common error statuses (a shared \\`responses=\\` default on the routers, or an \\`openapi()\\` override that rewrites the 422), regenerate the spec and client, and extend \\`backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\\` so every operation's 4xx responses use the envelope.\" 2>&1 | tail -1); I2=$(gh issue create --title \"dataq-client: file downloads return File with no file name or media type\" --label \"enhancement,priority/P3\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 7 — polish: MCP & API, performance, accessibility\" --body \"Found reviewing #2515. \\`download_comparison_report\\` now returns \\`File(payload=BytesIO(response.content))\\`, but the generator fills neither \\`file_name\\` nor \\`mime_type\\`, so a \\`sync()\\` caller cannot tell CSV from XLSX or recover the \\`comparison-<id>.<fmt>\\` name without dropping to \\`sync_detailed()\\` and reading the headers. A hand-written convenience method in \\`packages/dataq-client/src/dataq_client/client.py\\` (like \\`export_suite_yaml\\`) that fills both from \\`Content-Type\\` and \\`Content-Disposition\\` would close it.\" 2>&1 | tail -1); echo \"$I1 $I2\"","description":"Regenerate, run drift checks and tests, fix the fragment, file two issues","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":892,"cache_read_input_tokens":669551,"output_tokens":1642,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":85},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":892,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1642,"cache_read_input_tokens":669551,"cache_creation_input_tokens":892,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":892},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01D1SHQVV9fMRaAsJsZ2NqZ5":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && /bin/bash -c 'u=$(grep \"^POSTGRES_USER=\" .env | cut -d= -f2); p=$(grep \"^POSTGRES_PASSWORD=\"REDACTED\"REDACTED\"; $B/python -m backend.scripts.export_docs_reference >/dev/null 2>&1; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-arijit-Coding-Python-DataQ/641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d/scratchpad/ruff0165; PATH=\"$S/bin:$PATH\" $B/python scripts/generate-dataq-client.py >/dev/null 2>&1; PATH=\"$S/bin:$PATH\" $B/python scripts/generate-dataq-client.py --check >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"client rc=$?\"; $B/python -m backend.scripts.export_docs_reference --check >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"export rc=$?\"; $B/python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov backend/tests -k \"comparison or openapi or test_main\" 2>&1 | tail -1'; printf '%s\\n' \"**The comparison-report download is described correctly in the API reference.** It was documented as returning JSON, so the generated Python client failed on every download; the reference now lists its CSV and XLSX media types and the client returns the downloaded file.\" > changelog.d/2514.fixed.md; I1=$(gh issue create --title \"OpenAPI: no operation declares its error responses, and every 422 is typed as FastAPI's HTTPValidationError instead of the DataQ error envelope\" --label \"bug,priority/P2\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 7 — polish: MCP & API, performance, accessibility\" --body \"Found reviewing #2515. None of the 170 operations in \\`docs/site/reference/openapi.json\\` declares a 4xx response other than the auto-added 422, and that 422 is typed as \\`HTTPValidationError\\` while \\`core/errors.py\\`'s handlers return \\`{\\\"error\\\": {\\\"code\\\", \\\"message\\\", \\\"detail\\\"}}\\` (\\`ErrorResponse\\`).\n\nEffect on the generated \\`dataq-client\\`: a 404/403/409 parses to \\`None\\` (or raises only with \\`raise_on_unexpected_status\\`), and a 422 is parsed by \\`HTTPValidationError.from_dict\\`, which finds no \\`detail\\` key and returns an empty object, so the server's message is lost.\n\nFix: register \\`ErrorResponse\\` as the response model for the common error statuses (a shared \\`responses=\\` default on the routers, or an \\`openapi()\\` override that rewrites the 422), regenerate the spec and client, and extend \\`backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\\` so every operation's 4xx responses use the envelope.\" 2>&1 | tail -1); I2=$(gh issue create --title \"dataq-client: file downloads return File with no file name or media type\" --label \"enhancement,priority/P3\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 7 — polish: MCP & API, performance, accessibility\" --body \"Found reviewing #2515. \\`download_comparison_report\\` now returns \\`File(payload=BytesIO(response.content))\\`, but the generator fills neither \\`file_name\\` nor \\`mime_type\\`, so a \\`sync()\\` caller cannot tell CSV from XLSX or recover the \\`comparison-<id>.<fmt>\\` name without dropping to \\`sync_detailed()\\` and reading the headers. A hand-written convenience method in \\`packages/dataq-client/src/dataq_client/client.py\\` (like \\`export_suite_yaml\\`) that fills both from \\`Content-Type\\` and \\`Content-Disposition\\` would close it.\" 2>&1 | tail -1); echo \"$I1 $I2\"","description":"Regenerate, run drift checks and tests, fix the fragment, file two issues","timeout":600000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01D1SHQVV9fMRaAsJsZ2NqZ5":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f3f6b978-a86e-4b88-b4fe-4fd6f97923f0","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgEpmdAU4eRdafrxE7naG","requestRef":"d5037789-c13b-44a5-90db-d0543a718f5f","requestedModel":"claude-