{"parentUuid":"428342be-e43e-49f4-be89-a20b0ee64603","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"85d36563-d90f-4bb8-9f21-dc3d273fab41","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:24:42.821Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","hash":"8c63f0929d85fa304c6969187259f46342a7bf7bf5190ccf202a694b3ab1c136","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Both halves of the fix are now caught. Regenerating artifacts, fixing the changelog wording, and filing the two deferred findings."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D1SHQVV9fMRaAsJsZ2NqZ5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && /bin/bash -c 'u=$(grep \"^POSTGRES_USER=\" .env | cut -d= -f2); p=$(grep \"^POSTGRES_PASSWORD=\"REDACTED\"REDACTED\"; $B/python -m backend.scripts.export_docs_reference >/dev/null 2>&1; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-arijit-Coding-Python-DataQ/641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d/scratchpad/ruff0165; PATH=\"$S/bin:$PATH\" $B/python scripts/generate-dataq-client.py >/dev/null 2>&1; PATH=\"$S/bin:$PATH\" $B/python scripts/generate-dataq-client.py --check >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"client rc=$?\"; $B/python -m backend.scripts.export_docs_reference --check >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"export rc=$?\"; $B/python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov backend/tests -k \"comparison or openapi or test_main\" 2>&1 | tail -1'; printf '%s\\n' \"**The comparison-report download is described correctly in the API reference.** It was documented as returning JSON, so the generated Python client failed on every download; the reference now lists its CSV and XLSX media types and the client returns the downloaded file.\" > changelog.d/2514.fixed.md; I1=$(gh issue create --title \"OpenAPI: no operation declares its error responses, and every 422 is typed as FastAPI's HTTPValidationError instead of the DataQ error envelope\" --label \"bug,priority/P2\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 7 — polish: MCP & API, performance, accessibility\" --body \"Found reviewing #2515. None of the 170 operations in \\`docs/site/reference/openapi.json\\` declares a 4xx response other than the auto-added 422, and that 422 is typed as \\`HTTPValidationError\\` while \\`core/errors.py\\`'s handlers return \\`{\\\"error\\\": {\\\"code\\\", \\\"message\\\", \\\"detail\\\"}}\\` (\\`ErrorResponse\\`).\n\nEffect on the generated \\`dataq-client\\`: a 404/403/409 parses to \\`None\\` (or raises only with \\`raise_on_unexpected_status\\`), and a 422 is parsed by \\`HTTPValidationError.from_dict\\`, which finds no \\`detail\\` key and returns an empty object, so the server's message is lost.\n\nFix: register \\`ErrorResponse\\` as the response model for the common error statuses (a shared \\`responses=\\` default on the routers, or an \\`openapi()\\` override that rewrites the 422), regenerate the spec and client, and extend \\`backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\\` so every operation's 4xx responses use the envelope.\" 2>&1 | tail -1); I2=$(gh issue create --title \"dataq-client: file downloads return File with no file name or media type\" --label \"enhancement,priority/P3\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 7 — polish: MCP & API, performance, accessibility\" --body \"Found reviewing #2515. \\`download_comparison_report\\` now returns \\`File(payload=BytesIO(response.content))\\`, but the generator fills neither \\`file_name\\` nor \\`mime_type\\`, so a \\`sync()\\` caller cannot tell CSV from XLSX or recover the \\`comparison-<id>.<fmt>\\` name without dropping to \\`sync_detailed()\\` and reading the headers. A hand-written convenience method in \\`packages/dataq-client/src/dataq_client/client.py\\` (like \\`export_suite_yaml\\`) that fills both from \\`Content-Type\\` and \\`Content-Disposition\\` would close it.\" 2>&1 | tail -1); echo \"$I1 $I2\"","description":"Regenerate, run drift checks and tests, fix the fragment, file two issues","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
