{"parentUuid":"0e306c99-44d4-4c63-89b9-3a3b45d0168d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEptnRGinn2d7vxo28fe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X6mTe1V6Yu9o6JKEnfs6aK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"C=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD); r(){ gh api graphql -f query='mutation($t:ID!,$b:String!){addPullRequestReviewThreadReply(input:{pullRequestReviewThreadId:$t,body:$b}){comment{id}}}' -f t=\"$1\" -f b=\"$2\" >/dev/null && gh api graphql -f query='mutation($t:ID!){resolveReviewThread(input:{threadId:$t}){thread{isResolved}}}' -f t=\"$1\" -q .data.resolveReviewThread.thread.isResolved; }\nr PRRT_kwDOSBITx86uojPI \"Fixed in $C: \\`test_every_file_download_is_mapped_for_the_client\\` reads \\`openapi-config.yaml\\` and fails on a binary body not mapped to octet-stream, or a success response with no media the client can parse. Reverting either the overrides or the route makes it fail (checked).\"\nr PRRT_kwDOSBITx86uojQM \"Filed as #2518: no operation declares its error responses, and the 422 is typed as HTTPValidationError app-wide. Fixing one route alone would leave the spec inconsistent.\"\nr PRRT_kwDOSBITx86uojQ9 \"Fixed in $C: \\`REPORT_MEDIA_TYPES\\` in \\`services/comparison_report.py\\` is the one source; the route builds its declared content from it and \\`build_report\\` returns from it. The client mapping is held to it by the contract test.\"\nr PRRT_kwDOSBITx86uojR8 \"Fixed in $C: every 2xx response is checked; a typed 201 beside an untyped 200 is refused (parametrised case).\"\nr PRRT_kwDOSBITx86uojTB \"Fixed in $C: a schema must carry type, \\$ref, allOf/anyOf/oneOf, enum or const; a title-only schema is refused (parametrised case).\"\nr PRRT_kwDOSBITx86uojUp \"Fixed in $C: the summary check is removed; \\`test_main.py::test_every_api_endpoint_has_summary_and_tags\\` holds it, and the module docstring points there.\"\nr PRRT_kwDOSBITx86uojV7 \"Filed as #2519 (a hand-written convenience method like \\`export_suite_yaml\\` that fills name and media type). The changelog fragment now says the client returns the downloaded file, not bytes.\"","description":"Reply to and resolve the seven #2515 threads"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1061,"cache_read_input_tokens":672243,"output_tokens":921,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1061,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":921,"cache_read_input_tokens":672243,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1061},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01X6mTe1V6Yu9o6JKEnfs6aK":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && C=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD); r(){ gh api graphql -f query='mutation($t:ID!,$b:String!){addPullRequestReviewThreadReply(input:{pullRequestReviewThreadId:$t,body:$b}){comment{id}}}' -f t=\"$1\" -f b=\"$2\" >/dev/null && gh api graphql -f query='mutation($t:ID!){resolveReviewThread(input:{threadId:$t}){thread{isResolved}}}' -f t=\"$1\" -q .data.resolveReviewThread.thread.isResolved; }\nr PRRT_kwDOSBITx86uojPI \"Fixed in $C: \\`test_every_file_download_is_mapped_for_the_client\\` reads \\`openapi-config.yaml\\` and fails on a binary body not mapped to octet-stream, or a success response with no media the client can parse. Reverting either the overrides or the route makes it fail (checked).\"\nr PRRT_kwDOSBITx86uojQM \"Filed as #2518: no operation declares its error responses, and the 422 is typed as HTTPValidationError app-wide. Fixing one route alone