{"parentUuid":"d831f16d-33dd-4f69-a0b9-e335cfb5bdd8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEpw45RK6j9nFSPX637G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QbyamaYuwQzSQoKJggJckj","name":"Skill","input":{"skill":"code-review","args":"2512 --comment medium"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_read_input_tokens":673304,"output_tokens":235,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":118},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":235,"cache_read_input_tokens":673304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QbyamaYuwQzSQoKJggJckj":{"skill":"code-review","args":"2512 --comment medium"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e377fec2-6a28-47d9-a672-073a1b6ba35f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgEpw3eczfEesmoCr8Fj8","requestRef":"137b91f1-cc7e-4a64-ac6a-ab5ac0f153d1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1b42278-9c52-4c4b-b203-56836602c442","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:26:14.903Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
{"parentUuid":"f1b42278-9c52-4c4b-b203-56836602c442","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"429dd6a2-e50c-4f9b-bdde-be5a4b9a7a7c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QbyamaYuwQzSQoKJggJckj","content":"Skill \"code-review\" completed (forked execution).\n\nResult:\nI reviewed PR #2512 and found 8 issues, none of them a runtime bug. Seven are posted as inline comments; the rule 11 one is a general PR comment because line 88 is outside the diff (the inline post got HTTP 422). The PR has three parts: rules 44–45 in `CONTRIBUTING.md`, a new standards checklist in the PR template, and a new guard test, `backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py`. Most findings are gaps in what that test actually enforces, or wrong references in the new rules.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py\",\"line\":57,\"summary\":\"The 'vendor exporter only in core/otel.py' guard only checks `azure.monitor`. OTLP and other `opentelemetry.exporter.*` or vendor-extension imports are allowed in all four `_OTEL_SEAM` files.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"An OTLP gRPC exporter or a GCP/AWS exporter imported in core/tracing.py or core/usage_telemetry.py passes every test, though rule 45 says exporting happens only from core/otel.py.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py\",\"line\":34,\"summary\":\"The AST scan only sees static `import` statements, so `importlib.import_module(...)` or `__import__(...)` gets past every boundary test.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"`importlib.import_module(\\\"sentry_sdk\\\").init(...)` in main.py passes `test_no_proprietary_telemetry_sdk_is_imported`.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\"line\":190,\"summary\":\"Rule 44 says secrets and PII follow 'sections E and H', but H is the security-review cadence. Secrets are in section C (rules 15/15a) and PII redaction in section E (rule 27).\",\"failure_scenario\":\"A contributor looking for the secret bar reads section H and misses betterleaks and the no-credentials rules.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\"line\":191,\"summary\":\"Rule 45 names `backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py` as the OpenAPI enforcement, but that file doesn't exist on this branch; it arrives with #2515.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"If this PR merges before #2515, main has a binding rule whose enforcing check doesn't exist.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\"line\":88,\"summary\":\"Rule 11 still lists the old PR-template checklist (manual test, linked issue, security implications, schema migration) and doesn't mention the new rules 44–45 section.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"A reader of rule 11 doesn't learn the new standards checklist exists.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py\",\"line\":18,\"summary\":\"`_PROPRIETARY_TELEMETRY` is a short denylist that misses common APM SDKs such as elasticapm, logfire, rollbar, bugsnag, aws_xray_sdk and google.cloud.trace.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"Adding aws_xray_sdk or elasticapm passes, against rule 45's 'no proprietary APM SDK is added'.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py\",\"line\":61,\"summary\":\"`_imports()` re-reads and re-parses all of backend/app on every call: 8 times in the proprietary-SDK test alone, about 12 times per run.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"Every pytest run does avoidable parsing work. Fix: `@functools.cache` on `_imports()` with a tuple return.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py\",\"line\":34,\"summary\":\"`read_text()` has no `encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"`, so it decodes with the locale encoding.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"On a machine with a non-UTF-8 locale (LANG=C, Windows cp1252), source files with em-dashes raise UnicodeDecodeError and all five tests error out.\"}\n]\n```"}]},"uuid":"afd00fa3-5729-45ef-9445-70272719c261","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:28:32.800Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"commandName":"code-review","status":"forked","agentId":"a2649772b81b597bb","result":"I reviewed PR #2512 and found 8 issues, none of them a runtime bug. Seven are posted as inline comments; the rule 11 one is a general PR comment because line 88 is outside the diff (the inline post got HTTP 422). The PR has three parts: rules 44–45 in `CONTRIBUTING.md`, a new standards checklist in the PR template, and a new guard test, `backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py`. Most findings are gaps in what that test actually enforces, or wrong references in the new rules.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py\",\"line\":57,\"summary\":\"The 'vendor exporter only in core/otel.py' guard only checks `azure.monitor`. OTLP and other `opentelemetry.exporter.*` or vendor-extension imports are allowed in all four `_OTEL_SEAM` files.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"An OTLP gRPC exporter or a GCP/AWS exporter imported in core/tracing.py or core/usage_telemetry.py passes every test, though rule 45 says exporting happens only from core/otel.py.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py\",\"line\":34,\"summary\":\"The AST scan only sees static `import` statements, so `importlib.import_module(...)` or `__import__(...)` gets past every boundary test.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"`importlib.import_module(\\\"sentry_sdk\\\").init(...)` in main.py passes `test_no_proprietary_telemetry_sdk_is_imported`.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\"line\":190,\"summary\":\"Rule 44 says secrets and PII follow 'sections E and H', but H is the security-review cadence. Secrets are in section C (rules 15/15a) and PII redaction in section E (rule 27).\",\"failure_scenario\":\"A contributor looking for the secret bar reads section H and misses betterleaks and the no-credentials rules.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\"line\":191,\"summary\":\"Rule 45 names `backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py` as the OpenAPI enforcement, but that file doesn't exist on this branch; it arrives with #2515.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"If this PR merges before #2515, main has a binding rule whose enforcing check doesn't exist.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\"line\":88,\"summary\":\"Rule 11 still lists the old PR-template checklist (manual test, linked issue, security implications, schema migration) and doesn't mention the new rules 44–45 section.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"A reader of rule 11 doesn't learn the new standards checklist exists.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py\",\"line\":18,\"summary\":\"`_PROPRIETARY_TELEMETRY` is a short denylist that misses common APM SDKs such as elasticapm, logfire, rollbar, bugsnag, aws_xray_sdk and google.cloud.trace.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"Adding aws_xray_sdk or elasticapm passes, against rule 45's 'no proprietary APM SDK is added'.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py\",\"line\":61,\"summary\":\"`_imports()` re-reads and re-parses all of backend/app on every call: 8 times in the proprietary-SDK test alone, about 12 times per run.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"Every pytest run does avoidable parsing work. Fix: `@functools.cache` on `_imports()` with a tuple return.\"},\n  {\"file\":\"backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py\",\"line\":34,\"summary\":\"`read_text()` has no `encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"`, so it decodes with the locale encoding.\",\"failure_scenario\":\"On a machine with a non-UTF-8 locale (LANG=C, Windows cp1252), source files with em-dashes raise UnicodeDecodeError and all five tests error out.\"}\n]\n```"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e377fec2-6a28-47d9-a672-073a1b6ba35f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","root":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","branch":"fix/openapi-contract-gate","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"publi