{"parentUuid":"07e84211-3ca3-4f60-bfd5-b055bad8e5ee","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"429dd6a2-e50c-4f9b-bdde-be5a4b9a7a7c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011sEKtUmkeTFn1eXzo8tehu","type":"tool_result","content":"11. **PR template** checklist (`.github/pull_request_template.md`): manual test ✓, linked issue, security implications, schema migration.\nlate** checklist (`.github/pull_request_template.md`): manual test ✓, linked issue, security implications, schema migration. Its *Standards for new code* section is the checklist for rules 44–45.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8a9bae3e-f29b-46c8-8ce8-86c1a51d4180","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:28:50.615Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"11. **PR template** checklist (`.github/pull_request_template.md`): manual test ✓, linked issue, security implications, schema migration.\nlate** checklist (`.github/pull_request_template.md`): manual test ✓, linked issue, security implications, schema migration. Its *Standards for new code* section is the checklist for rules 44–45.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CONTRIBUTING.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":85,"oldLines":7,"newStart":85,"newLines":7,"lines":["     - `ci:` — CI/CD workflow changes","     - Format: `<type>(<optional scope>): <short imperative description>`","     - Examples: `feat(api): add suite dry-run endpoint`, `fix(celery): handle graceful shutdown on SIGTERM`","-11. **PR template** checklist (`.github/pull_request_template.md`): manual test ✓, linked issue, security implications, schema migration.","+11. **PR template** checklist (`.github/pull_request_template.md`): manual test ✓, linked issue, security implications, schema migration. Its *Standards for new code* section is the checklist for rules 44–45."," 12. **`CODEOWNERS`** (`.github/CODEOWNERS`) auto-routes reviews per area."," "," ---"]},{"oldStart":187,"oldLines":7,"newStart":187,"newLines":7,"lines":[" 41. **Published docs (`docs/site/`, the `docs_dir` GitHub Pages build) never cite issue IDs or PR numbers** — no `#NNNN`, no `github.com/.../issues/…` or `/pull/…` links. Those are internal project-tracking artifacts with no meaning to an external reader of the public site; state the *behavior*, not the ticket that produced it. Also don't link a published page to an un-published internal doc (`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/progress*.md`, `docs/retro*.md`, `docs/ops-log.md`) — those aren't reachable from the site and the link is dead weight for a reader outside the repo. Minimize cross-links from ordinary published pages into `docs/site/adr/` too: ADRs are design-rationale records for contributors, not the audience of a feature guide — link one only when the ADR itself is the answer to what the reader is asking, not as a routine \"see also.\" **Within `docs/site/adr/`:** ADR-to-ADR references are fine (an ADR is allowed to cite another ADR it supersedes/amends/depends on — that's the decision graph, not project tracking). ADR-to-PR references should still be minimized — an ADR records *why a decision was made*, not *which PR shipped it*; a PR link ties a durable rationale to an ephemeral implementation artifact and is exactly the class rule 41 exists to keep out."," 42. **Stable external surfaces follow the API compatibility policy** (`docs/site/reference/api-compatibility.md`): the REST API, MCP tools, the suite export document and the Python client (`dataq-client` and its CLI). An additive change needs nothing; a breaking change is announced under **Breaking** in the CHANGELOG, stays deprecated for at least one minor release before removal (security fixes excepted, still announced), and any suite-document shape change (an added field included) bumps its `version` while the previous version stays importable for a minor release. A PR that changes a stable surface says which kind of change it is."," 43. **Changelog entries are fragments, assembled at release.** A PR never edits the Unreleased part of `docs/site/reference/changelog.md`; it adds `changelog.d/<issue>.<section>.md` (`<issue>-<n>` for a second entry; section one of `breaking | security | added | changed | fixed`; body = the bullet's text without the leading `- `, bold lead phrase, no ticket numbers — rule 41). The published page renders them under **Unreleased** at build time (`docs/hooks/changelog_fragments.py`). CI fails a PR that touches user-facing paths (`backend/app/`, `frontend/src/`, `packages/`, `integrations/`, `deploy/`, `docs/site/{guides,get-started,reference}/`) without a fragment unless it carries the **`no-changelog`** label; Dependabot is exempt. At release, `python scripts/changelog.py assemble --version X.Y.Z --date YYYY-MM-DD` moves the fragments into the dated section (the step is in the release checklist, `docs/site/operate/runbook-faq.md`). Grammar and examples: `changelog.d/README.md`.","-44. **New code meets the standards already in force; a known gap is not a licence to widen it.** Open debt (the Week-7 accessibility audits #1672/#1673, any filed backlog item) is fixed on its own schedule, but a PR adds nothing to it. For UI, beyond rule 4b's automated floor: every new control is reachable and operable by keyboard, a dialog or drawer takes focus on open and returns it on close, every control and icon button has an accessible name, status that changes without navigation (a run, a save, an async result) is announced through a live region, a chart has a text or table alternative, colours come from the theme tokens in both themes, a new click-to-navigate row gets a `keyboard.spec.ts` case, and the change is checked in the browser's accessibility tree rather than the DOM. For the other surfaces, the existing bars apply to new code without exception: MCP tools state their blind spots (the `mcp-honesty-reviewer` agent on any change to `backend/app/mcp/server.py`), migrations follow rules 30–31 (the `migration-safety` agent), dependencies pass rule 40's licence gate, published docs follow rule 41, values crossing a driver boundary are tested in the shape the driver returns (the `driver-boundary-guard` agent), and secrets and PII follow sections E and H. Where a standard cannot be met in the PR, the PR says which and links the filed issue.","+44. **New code meets the standards already in force; a known gap is not a licence to widen it.** Open debt (the Week-7 accessibility audits #1672/#1673, any filed backlog item) is fixed on its own schedule, but a PR adds nothing to it. For UI, beyond rule 4b's automated floor: every new control is reachable and operable by keyboard, a dialog or drawer takes focus on open and returns it on close, every control and icon button has an accessible name, status that changes without navigation (a run, a save, an async result) is announced through a live region, a chart has a text or table alternative, colours come from the theme tokens in both themes, a new click-to-navigate row gets a `keyboard.spec.ts` case, and the change is checked in the browser's accessibility tree rather than the DOM. For the other surfaces, the existing bars apply to new code without exception: MCP tools state their blind spots (the `mcp-honesty-reviewer` agent on any change to `backend/app/mcp/server.py`), migrations follow rules 30–31 (the `migration-safety` agent), dependencies pass rule 40's licence gate, published docs follow rule 41, values crossing a driver boundary are tested in the shape the driver returns (the `driver-boundary-guard` agent), and secrets and PII follow rules 15, 15a and 27 and the review cadence in section H. Where a standard cannot be met in the PR, the PR says which and links the filed issue."," 45. **Interfaces use the open standard that exists for them, and the check that enforces it stays green.** **OpenAPI:** every REST operation has a summary and a typed success response (`backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py`), a file download declares its media types, and `docs/site/reference/openapi.json` plus the generated `dataq-client` are regenerated in the same PR (both drift checks run in CI). **OpenTelemetry:** traces, logs and metrics are emitted through the OTel SDK and exported over OTLP from `core/otel.py`; a vendor exporter lives only there, no proprietary APM SDK is added, attributes follow the OTel semantic conventions with DataQ's own under `dataq.*`, and usage events go through the closed vocabulary in `core/usage_telemetry.py` (`backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py` holds the import boundary). **OpenLineage:** lineage events are OpenLineage run events built in `backend/app/lineage/` (same test). **ODCS:** a data contract is read and written as an Open Data Contract Standard document (current major, v3); DataQ-specific fields go in its custom properties, never a parallel format. **OIDC** for sign-in, **SPDX** for the SBOM, the **Vault KV v2 API** for the secret store, **conventional commits** and the API compatibility policy (rule 42) for versioning. A new interface with no fitting standard records that in its ADR."," "," ---"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CONTRIBUTING.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"04f6a76d-8227-4140-80f1-928330cf9a34","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","root":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","branch":"docs/new-code-meets-standards","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"07e84211-3ca3-4f60-bfd5-b055bad8e5ee","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
