{"parentUuid":"95839f07-f53a-496b-aac1-01f900232449","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"429dd6a2-e50c-4f9b-bdde-be5a4b9a7a7c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018KG4jsX4zpUmeAmhWKe9RB","type":"tool_result","content":"true\ntrue\ntrue\ntrue\ntrue\ntrue\ntrue\ndone","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2a95063c-1f36-49a6-a8c8-64adde489f5b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:30:46.989Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"true\ntrue\ntrue\ntrue\ntrue\ntrue\ntrue\ndone","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/.github/pull_request_template.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":52,"oldLines":17,"newStart":52,"newLines":6,"lines":[" - [ ] **`docs/progress.md` — N/A** for this PR"," - [ ] **Security implications considered** (auth, input validation, secret handling, PII in logs)"," ","-## Standards for new code (CONTRIBUTING rules 44–45)","-","-<!-- Tick what applies; write N/A beside a group that does not. A standard the PR cannot meet is named here with its filed issue. -->","-- [ ] **UI a11y:** new controls work by keyboard; dialogs and drawers take and return focus; every control has an accessible name; async status is announced (live region); charts have a text or table alternative; theme tokens only, both themes; new routes scanned (rule 4b) and new click-to-navigate rows have a `keyboard.spec.ts` case; checked in the accessibility tree","-- [ ] **MCP:** `mcp-honesty-reviewer` run on any `backend/app/mcp/server.py` change; sibling docstrings re-read","-- [ ] **Migrations:** `migration-safety` run; single alembic head after merging `main`","-- [ ] **Dependencies:** pinned in the single source of truth; licence gate passes","-- [ ] **Driver boundary:** values from a driver/SDK tested in the shape it returns (`driver-boundary-guard`)","-- [ ] **Published docs:** no ticket or internal-doc references; counts checked against the code","-- [ ] **Open standards (rule 45):** REST changes keep `openapi.json` and `dataq-client` regenerated with typed responses; telemetry only through the OTel seam; lineage as OpenLineage; contracts as ODCS","-"," ## Schema migration?"," "," - [ ] No schema change"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CLAUDE.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":158,"oldLines":7,"newStart":158,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## 6. Working agreements (rules above feature work)"," ","-Full list (45 rules across 8 categories) lives in [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Highlights:","+Full list (42 rules across 8 categories) lives in [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Highlights:"," "," ### Commit & change discipline"," Per-functionality workflow, in order:"]},{"oldStart":213,"oldLines":7,"newStart":213,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## 7. Required reading before coding"," ","-1. [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — full 45-rule working agreements + DoD + commit/branch conventions","+1. [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — full 42-rule working agreements + DoD + commit/branch conventions"," 2. [docs/site/adr/](docs/site/adr/) — all ADRs (architecture decisions with rationale)"," 3. [context/DataQ_platform_roadmap.md](context/DataQ_platform_roadmap.md) — the 8-week, 100-task product roadmap"," 4. The current week's milestone target (see §13 below)"]},{"oldStart":287,"oldLines":7,"newStart":287,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Story ledger (curated narrative wins — internal) | [docs/stories.md](docs/stories.md) |"," | System architecture diagram | [docs/site/architecture/overview.md](docs/site/architecture/overview.md) |"," | Architecture Decision Records | [docs/site/adr/](docs/site/adr/) |","-| Working agreements (full 45-rule list) | [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) |","+| Working agreements (full 42-rule list) | [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) |"," | Live task tracker (post-v1, per-PR status) | [docs/progress.md](docs/progress.md) — completed ledgers are archived at [docs/progress-v1.md](docs/progress-v1.md), [docs/progress-v1.1.md](docs/progress-v1.1.md) and [docs/progress-v1.2.md](docs/progress-v1.2.md) |"," | **Deploy runbook + pre-/post-deploy checklists** | [deploy/README.md](deploy/README.md) — provisioning, the `workflow_dispatch` Deploy flow, and the **pre-deploy** (CI green, docs current, migration-safe) + **post-deploy smoke** (login, UI renders, every high-level flow works, infra rolled) checklists. **Run both around every deploy.** |"," | **Static read-only demo** (Pages `/demo/`, #2419) | [frontend/e2e-demo/README.md](frontend/e2e-demo/README.md) — the real SPA built with `VITE_DEMO`, answering from API responses that CI's `frontend-e2e` job records off the seeded stack on every run (never committed); `publish-demo` republishes on each push to `main`. **A new `<Route>` must be added to `e2e-demo/routes.ts`** (a Vitest check fails otherwise). |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CONTRIBUTING.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":85,"oldLines":7,"newStart":85,"newLines":7,"lines":["     - `ci:` — CI/CD workflow changes","     - Format: `<type>(<optional scope>): <short imperative description>`","     - Examples: `feat(api): add suite dry-run endpoint`, `fix(celery): handle graceful shutdown on SIGTERM`","-11. **PR template** checklist (`.github/pull_request_template.md`): manual test ✓, linked issue, security implications, schema migration. Its *Standards for new code* section is the checklist for rules 44–45.","+11. **PR template** checklist (`.github/pull_request_template.md`): manual test ✓, linked issue, security implications, schema migration."," 12. **`CODEOWNERS`** (`.github/CODEOWNERS`) auto-routes reviews per area."," "," ---"]},{"oldStart":187,"oldLines":8,"newStart":187,"newLines":6,"lines":[" 41. **Published docs (`docs/site/`, the `docs_dir` GitHub Pages build) never cite issue IDs or PR numbers** — no `#NNNN`, no `github.com/.../issues/…` or `/pull/…` links. Those are internal project-tracking artifacts with no meaning to an external reader of the public site; state the *behavior*, not the ticket that produced it. Also don't link a published page to an un-published internal doc (`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/progress*.md`, `docs/retro*.md`, `docs/ops-log.md`) — those aren't reachable from the site and the link is dead weight for a reader outside the repo. Minimize cross-links from ordinary published pages into `docs/site/adr/` too: ADRs are design-rationale records for contributors, not the audience of a feature guide — link one only when the ADR itself is the answer to what the reader is asking, not as a routine \"see also.\" **Within `docs/site/adr/`:** ADR-to-ADR references are fine (an ADR is allowed to cite another ADR it supersedes/amends/depends on — that's the decision graph, not project tracking). ADR-to-PR references should still be minimized — an ADR records *why a decision was made*, not *which PR shipped it*; a PR link ties a durable rationale to an ephemeral implementation artifact and is exactly the class rule 41 exists to keep out."," 42. **Stable external surfaces follow the API compatibility policy** (`docs/site/reference/api-compatibility.md`): the REST API, MCP tools, the suite export document and the Python client (`dataq-client` and its CLI). An additive change needs nothing; a breaking change is announced under **Breaking** in the CHANGELOG, stays deprecated for at least one minor release before removal (security fixes excepted, still announced), and any suite-document shape change (an added field included) bumps its `version` while the previous version stays importable for a minor release. A PR that changes a stable surface says which kind of change it is."," 43. **Changelog entries are fragments, assembled at release.** A PR never edits the Unreleased part of `docs/site/reference/changelog.md`; it adds `changelog.d/<issue>.<section>.md` (`<issue>-<n>` for a second entry; section one of `breaking | security | added | changed | fixed`; body = the bullet's text without the leading `- `, bold lead phrase, no ticket numbers — rule 41). The published page renders them under **Unreleased** at build time (`docs/hooks/changelog_fragments.py`). CI fails a PR that touches user-facing paths (`backend/app/`, `frontend/src/`, `packages/`, `integrations/`, `deploy/`, `docs/site/{guides,get-started,reference}/`) without a fragment unless it carries the **`no-changelog`** label; Dependabot is exempt. At release, `python scripts/changelog.py assemble --version X.Y.Z --date YYYY-MM-DD` moves the fragments into the dated section (the step is in the release checklist, `docs/site/operate/runbook-faq.md`). Grammar and examples: `changelog.d/README.md`.","-44. **New code meets the standards already in force; a known gap is not a licence to widen it.** Open debt (the Week-7 accessibility audits #1672/#1673, any filed backlog item) is fixed on its own schedule, but a PR adds nothing to it. For UI, beyond rule 4b's automated floor: every new control is reachable and operable by keyboard, a dialog or drawer takes focus on open and returns it on close, every control and icon button has an accessible name, status that changes without navigation (a run, a save, an async result) is announced through a live region, a chart has a text or table alternative, colours come from the theme tokens in both themes, a new click-to-navigate row gets a `keyboard.spec.ts` case, and the change is checked in the browser's accessibility tree rather than the DOM. For the other surfaces, the existing bars apply to new code without exception: MCP tools state their blind spots (the `mcp-honesty-reviewer` agent on any change to `backend/app/mcp/server.py`), migrations follow rules 30–31 (the `migration-safety` agent), dependencies pass rule 40's licence gate, published docs follow rule 41, values crossing a driver boundary are tested in the shape the driver returns (the `driver-boundary-guard` agent), and secrets and PII follow rules 15, 15a and 27 and the review cadence in section H. Where a standard cannot be met in the PR, the PR says which and links the filed issue.","-45. **Interfaces use the open standard that exists for them, and the check that enforces it stays green.** **OpenAPI:** every REST operation has a summary and a typed success response (`backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py`), a file download declares its media types, and `docs/site/reference/openapi.json` plus the generated `dataq-client` are regenerated in the same PR (both drift checks run in CI). **OpenTelemetry:** traces, logs and metrics are emitted through the OTel SDK and exported over OTLP from `core/otel.py`; a vendor exporter lives only there, no proprietary APM SDK is added, attributes follow the OTel semantic conventions with DataQ's own under `dataq.*`, and usage events go through the closed vocabulary in `core/usage_telemetry.py` (`backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py` holds the import boundary). **OpenLineage:** lineage events are OpenLineage run events built in `backend/app/lineage/` (same test). **ODCS:** a data contract is read and written as an Open Data Contract Standard document (current major, v3); DataQ-specific fields go in its custom properties, never a parallel format. **OIDC** for sign-in, **SPDX** for the SBOM, the **Vault KV v2 API** for the secret store, **conventional commits** and the API compatibility policy (rule 42) for versioning. A new interface with no fitting standard records that in its ADR."," "," ---"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/backend/app/datasources/flatfile.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":17,"oldLines":7,"newStart":17,"newLines":6,"lines":[" from backend.app.core.errors import SafeMonitorError"," from backend.app.core.logging import get_logger"," from backend.app.core.s3_endpoint import addressing_config_kwargs","-from backend.app.core.secrets import SecretStore"," from backend.app.datasources import jsonfile"," from backend.app.datasources.adls import AdlsConfig, blob_service_client"," from backend.app.datasources.base import ("]},{"oldStart":1480,"oldLines":55,"newStart":1479,"newLines":6,"lines":["         return SuiteOutcome(success=False, checks=merged)"," "," ","-def build_flatfile_runner(","-    *,","-    conn_type: str,","-    config: dict[str, Any],","-    secret_ref: str | None,","-    secret_store: SecretStore,","-    sampling: SampleSpec | None = None,","-) -> FlatFileCheckRunner:","-    \"\"\"Build a runner from a flat-file `Connection`'s primitives (secret resolved","-    eagerly; raw config, not the ORM model). ``sampling=None`` = whole-object read.","-    \"\"\"","-    if conn_type not in _FILE_TYPES:","-        raise ValueError(f\"{conn_type!r} is not a flat-file datasource\")","-    secret = resolve_flatfile_secret(","-        conn_type=conn_type, config=config, secret_ref=secret_ref, secret_store=secret_store","-    )","-    return FlatFileCheckRunner(conn_type=conn_type, config=config, secret=secret, sampling=sampling)","-","-","-class MissingCredentialError(ValueError):","-    \"\"\"The connection stores no credential and its auth mode needs one.\"\"\"","-","-","-def authenticates_without_secret(conn_type: str, config: dict[str, Any]) -> bool:","-    \"\"\"Whether a flat-file connection of this config needs no stored secret (GCS anonymous).\"\"\"","-    from backend.app.datasources.registry import authenticates_without_secret as answer","-","-    return answer(conn_type, config)","-","-","-def missing_credential(conn_type: str, config: dict[str, Any], secret_ref: str | None) -> bool:","-    \"\"\"The connection stores no credential and its auth mode needs one — the one rule every","-    flat-file caller checks before it reaches the store.\"\"\"","-    return not secret_ref and not authenticates_without_secret(conn_type, config)","-","-","-def resolve_flatfile_secret(","-    *,","-    conn_type: str,","-    config: dict[str, Any],","-    secret_ref: str | None,","-    secret_store: SecretStore,","-) -> str | None:","-    \"\"\"The credential every flat-file read presents, or ``None`` for an anonymous connection.\"\"\"","-    if missing_credential(conn_type, config, secret_ref):","-        raise MissingCredentialError(\"flat-file connection requires secret_ref for the credential\")","-    return secret_store.get(secret_ref) if secret_ref else None","-","-"," # ───────────────────────── batch resolution ────────────────────────"," # Batch pattern = regex whose FIRST capture group is the batch key; `latest`"," # takes the greatest key, `specific` a named one. Resolution is pure; only the"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/backend/app/datasources/registry.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":22,"oldLines":7,"newStart":22,"newLines":7,"lines":["     SampleSpec,","     TargetShapeError,"," )","-from backend.app.datasources.flatfile import build_flatfile_runner","+from backend.app.datasources.flatfile import FlatFileCheckRunner"," from backend.app.datasources.gcs import GcsConnectionAdapter"," from backend.app.datasources.generic_sql import (","     GenericSqlConnectionAdapter,"]},{"oldStart":102,"oldLines":6,"newStart":102,"newLines":50,"lines":["     return callable(requires) and not requires()"," "," ","+class MissingCredentialError(ValueError):","+    \"\"\"The connection stores no credential and its auth mode needs one.\"\"\"","+","+","+def missing_credential(conn_type: str, config: dict[str, Any], secret_ref: str | None) -> bool:","+    \"\"\"The connection stores no credential and its auth mode needs one: the one rule every","+    caller, flat-file or SQL, checks before it reaches the store. It and the flat-file secret","+    helpers below live here, not in ``flatfile``, because the rule is the adapters' to answer","+    and ``flatfile`` importing the registry would be an import cycle.\"\"\"","+    return not secret_ref and not authenticates_without_secret(conn_type, config)","+","+","+def resolve_flatfile_secret(","+    *,","+    conn_type: str,","+    config: dict[str, Any],","+    secret_ref: str | N