{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01L7KbEkDx4V7pgb2xKhFw23","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"a0bda4fd-a29f-4ebe-b5da-0249a6d1079d","ownerOrganizationUuid":"d338ef42-a650-40c7-a017-e1dca5ad4850"}
{"parentUuid":"70c78517-d861-4525-b35b-98d77ac5d7f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEqHxxvhchSLAv9PF7Nq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both PRs went through code review before merge, and every finding is either fixed or filed. CI is re-running on both. I'll merge #2515, then #2512, once they're green.\n\n**#2515, the OpenAPI gate.** Review found 7 issues.\n- **The main one:** my contract test would have passed the very bug it was meant to stop.\n  - The test now requires every success response to have a real schema.\n  - It also fails when a binary file download isn't mapped for the client generator.\n  - Reverting either half of the fix makes it fail, which I checked.\n- **One source for the report's file types:** the service and the route now both read them from the same list.\n- **Filed #2518:** no API operation declares its error responses, and every 422 is typed as FastAPI's default model instead of DataQ's error envelope. The generated client therefore loses the server's error message. That gap is app-wide, so it's a Week 7 item.\n- **Filed #2519:** downloaded files carry no filename or media type. That's a client convenience, also Week 7.\n\n**#2512, rules 44 and 45.** Review found 8 issues, all fixed.\n- **Exporter check:** it now catches any OpenTelemetry exporter imported outside its one allowed file, not only the Azure one.\n- **Dynamic imports:** `importlib.import_module` and `__import__` are now scanned too.\n- **SDK denylist:** it now covers 21 proprietary telemetry SDKs.\n- **Speed:** the test runs in 0.5 s instead of about 4 s.\n- **Wrong rule references:** rule 44 now points at the actual secret and PII rules.\n- **Rule 11:** it now points to the new checklist.\n\nInjecting a stray OpenTelemetry exporter and a dynamic Sentry import makes the right two tests fail, which I checked.\n\n**Merged:** #2513, which closes CodeQL alert #217.\n\n**Still running:** the audit of v1.3's UI against rule 44."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":587,"cache_read_input_tokens":682440,"output_tokens":642,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":587,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":682440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":587,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":587},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6c555a9f-2490-4e1b-a50a-8d5b977070a5","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEqHxQSWxQKVy8bbg1kz","requestRef":"9d0228dc-2998-4d1a-9bf8-69c65d27d3f4","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6cdc0cad-9274-4859-b33f-4e7ac1fce635","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:31:02.166Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
