{"parentUuid":"0d0a10c7-44f5-478e-a720-f650c343603f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEs4oUYLUBiLXM8rG6aZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The card spans the row cleanly at every width, there's no horizontal scroll, and axe finds no violations in either theme. Filing the conformance-report item, then opening the PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1144,"cache_read_input_tokens":702041,"output_tokens":1585,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":114},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1144,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1585,"cache_read_input_tokens":702041,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1144,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1144},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"cf589eeb-75a7-466d-b4f8-1e46bfc59688","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEs4nwnSh7RXoiPg3s9K","requestRef":"713d3992-4516-464c-8d2e-e6b865954e3e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9395fee4-67f5-49ea-b721-e403a79f16df","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:54:12.925Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/frontend","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"docs/a11y-marketing-claim"}
{"parentUuid":"9395fee4-67f5-49ea-b721-e403a79f16df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEs4oUYLUBiLXM8rG6aZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MfL9S37XAeR6brD5aRuetv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && N=$(gh issue create --title \"a11y: publish a WCAG 2.1 AA conformance report (ACR/VPAT) once the Week-7 audits close\" --label \"documentation,priority/P2\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 8 — test & dependency debt, decisions & cycle close\" --body \"Marketing and the docs landing now describe DataQ's accessibility checks without claiming conformance: automated scans in both themes, WCAG contrast ratios, non-colour status, keyboard navigation. A conformance claim (\\\"WCAG 2.1 AA\\\") needs more than an automated scan.\n\nScope once #1672 and #1673 are closed:\n- a manual pass with a screen reader (NVDA or VoiceOver) and keyboard only over every route, recorded per WCAG 2.1 A/AA success criterion;\n- an Accessibility Conformance Report in the VPAT 2.x format (WCAG edition), published under \\`docs/site/security/compliance/\\` or a sibling, with each criterion marked supports, partially supports or does not support, and the known exceptions;\n- after that, update the marketing card and docs-landing row to state the conformance level the report supports, and nothing more.\n\nDepends on: #1672, #1673, #2051.\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | grep -oE \"[0-9]+$\"); echo \"issue $N\"; git add -A marketing/index.html marketing/styles.css docs/site/index.md && git commit -q -m \"docs(marketing): describe the accessibility checks, without a conformance claim\n\nA 'Built with accessibility in mind' card on the marketing page and a row on the\ndocs landing state what is checked today. A lone last card now spans the grid\nrow. The deployment card names the Helm chart. A WCAG conformance claim waits\nfor the Week-7 audits and a conformance report (#$N).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1 | grep -iE \"failed|error\"; git push -q -u origin docs/a11y-marketing-claim 2>&1 | grep -iE \"error|rejected\"; gh pr create --title \"docs(marketing): describe the accessibility checks, without a conformance claim\" --body \"Maintainer direction (2026-10-21): mention accessibility in the marketing material, worded so it is true today.\n\n- **Marketing page.** A *Built with accessibility in mind* card. It says every page is checked for accessibility issues in both themes on every change, colour contrast is held to WCAG ratios, status never relies on colour alone, and core navigation works from the keyboard. It makes no WCAG, ADA or EAA conformance claim. That waits for the Week-7 audits (#1672, #1673) and the conformance report filed as #$N.\n- **Docs landing.** A matching row that says outright it describes the checks and is not a conformance claim.\n- **Layout.** The feature grid holds six cards in three columns. A seventh card spans the row (\\`:last-child:nth-child(3n + 1)\\`), so it never sits alone in one column.\n- **Deployment card.** It now names the Helm chart (#2505).\n\n**Checked (rule 44).** Headless Chromium at 1280, 900 and 375 px in both colour schemes. The card fills the row, there is no horizontal scroll, axe (WCAG 2 A/AA) finds no violations in the grid in either theme, and the card reads correctly in the accessibility tree. Docs guards and \\`mkdocs build --strict\\` pass.\n\n- N/A — marketing/docs copy (\\`no-changelog\\`)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" --label \"no-changelog,documentation\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 3 — datasources, deploy targets & auth\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git checkout -q main","description":"File the ACR issue, commit, and open the marketing PR","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1144,"cache_read_input_tokens":702041,"output_tokens":1585,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":114},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1144,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1585,"cache_read_input_tokens":702041,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1144,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1144},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MfL9S37XAeR6brD5aRuetv":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && N=$(gh issue create --title \"a11y: publish a WCAG 2.1 AA conformance report (ACR/VPAT) once the Week-7 audits close\" --label \"documentation,priority/P2\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 8 — test & dependency debt, decisions & cycle close\" --body \"Marketing and the docs landing now describe DataQ's accessibility checks without claiming conformance: automated scans in both themes, WCAG contrast ratios, non-colour status, keyboard navigation. A conformance claim (\\\"WCAG 2.1 AA\\\") needs more than an automated scan.\n\nScope once #1672 and #1673 are closed:\n- a manual pass with a screen reader (NVDA or VoiceOver) and keyboard only over every route, recorded per WCAG 2.1 A/AA success criterion;\n- an Accessibility Conformance Report in the VPAT 2.x format (WCAG edition), published under \\`docs/site/security/compliance/\\` or a sibling, with each criterion marked supports, partially supports or does not support, and the known exceptions;\n- after that, update the marketing card and docs-landing row to state the conformance level the report supports, and nothing more.\n\nDepends on: #1672, #1673, #2051.\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | grep -oE \"[0-9]+$\"); echo \"issue $N\"; git add -A marketing/index.html marketing/styles.css docs/site/index.md && git commit -q -m \"docs(marketing): describe the accessibility checks, without a conformance claim\n\nA 'Built with accessibility in mind' card on the marketing page and a row on the\ndocs landing state what is checked today. A lone last card now spans the grid\nrow. The deployment card names the Helm chart. A WCAG conformance claim waits\nfor the Week-7 audits and a conformance report (#$N).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1 | grep -iE \"failed|error\"; git push -q -u origin docs/a11y-marketing-claim 2>&1 | grep -iE \"error|rejected\"; gh pr create --title \"docs(marketing): describe the accessibility checks, without a conformance claim\" --body \"Maintainer direction (2026-10-21): mention accessibility in the marketing material, worded so it is true today.\n\n- **Marketing page.** A *Built with accessibility in mind* card. It says every page is checked for accessibility issues in both themes on every change, colour contrast is held to WCAG ratios, status never relies on colour alone, and core navigation works from the keyboard. It makes no WCAG, ADA or EAA conformance claim. That waits for the Week-7 audits (#1672, #1673) and the conformance report filed as #$N.\n- **Docs landing.** A matching row that says outright it describes the checks and is not a conformance claim.\n- **Layout.** The feature grid holds six cards in three columns. A seventh card spans the row (\\`:last-child:nth-child(3n + 1)\\`), so it never sits alone in one column.\n- **Deployment card.** It now names the Helm chart (#2505).\n\n**Checked (rule 44).** Headless Chromium at 1280, 900 and 375 px in both colour schemes. The card fills the row, there is no horizontal scroll, axe (WCAG 2 A/AA) finds no violations in the grid in either theme, and the card reads correctly in the accessibility tree. Docs guards and \\`mkdocs build --strict\\` pass.\n\n- N/A — marketing/docs copy (\\`no-changelog\\`)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" --label \"no-changelog,documentation\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 3 — datasources, deploy targets & auth\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git checkout -q main","description":"File the ACR issue, commit, and open the marketing PR","timeout":300000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"cf589eeb-75a7-466d-b4f8-1e46bfc59688","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgEs4nwnSh7RXoiPg3s9K","requestRef":"713d3992-4516-464c-8d2e-e6b865954e3e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"eb376dc4-b160-42f1-81df-10c0b2f34a9b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:54:24.492Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/frontend","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"docs/a11y-marketing-claim"}
