{"parentUuid":"4e169918-a347-41d9-8de4-2315bc39b762","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEs9EHu1pTXNx4ur4wnk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019NKP38pB5nRAiHkYQKgCyg","name":"Skill","input":{"skill":"code-review","args":"2521 --comment low"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1745,"cache_read_input_tokens":703185,"output_tokens":77,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1745,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":77,"cache_read_input_tokens":703185,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1745},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019NKP38pB5nRAiHkYQKgCyg":{"skill":"code-review","args":"2521 --comment low"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b192ec7d-e401-4915-8adc-f93cdbc7d0e1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEs9DX1HAwNbzDPUxevn","requestRef":"acb98407-7633-4630-97c1-458990507153","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"96ef59cd-2be1-4176-aaab-ba93b3406412","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:55:10.502Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"96ef59cd-2be1-4176-aaab-ba93b3406412","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"abc88b6b-0c7f-4068-93a6-b3c2a4b46c76","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_019NKP38pB5nRAiHkYQKgCyg","content":"Skill \"code-review\" completed (forked execution).\n\nResult:\nI reviewed PR #2521 and found six problems, all posted to the PR as inline comments. None is a code bug. Three are claims in the published copy that go further than what CI enforces, two are mismatches between the marketing page and the docs landing page, and one is a layout rule that will misplace cards if the count changes.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"marketing/index.html\",\n    \"line\": 195,\n    \"summary\": \"'status never relies on colour alone' is an absolute claim with no automated check behind it; axe doesn't detect it in general, and no test in rule 4b covers it.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Any chart, trend band, sparkline, tag or calendar cell that shows status by colour only makes the published marketing sentence false.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"marketing/index.html\",\n    \"line\": 195,\n    \"summary\": \"'Every page is checked' overclaims: the axe lanes scan only the app's routes, not the marketing site or the docs site.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A reader on the marketing page reasonably takes 'every page' to include that page and the docs, and neither is scanned. The same wording is on docs/site/index.md:73.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"marketing/index.html\",\n    \"line\": 195,\n    \"summary\": \"CI fails only on axe serious/critical violations (MIN_IMPACT in ratchet.ts), and CONTRIBUTING 4b says the SQL editor, lineage graph and drawer/modal focus return are not covered yet; the unqualified 'accessibility issues' reads as all issues.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A moderate or minor axe violation, or a focus-return bug in a modal, passes CI while the copy implies those pages were checked for it.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"docs/site/index.md\",\n    \"line\": 71,\n    \"summary\": \"The marketing deployment card now names the Helm chart (#2505), but the matching docs landing row was not updated.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Someone reading the docs landing doesn't learn that a Kubernetes/Helm path exists; the two published surfaces disagree.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"docs/site/index.md\",\n    \"line\": 73,\n    \"summary\": \"The docs row heading 'Use it from the keyboard, in either theme' doesn't match the marketing title 'Built with accessibility in mind', and is narrower than the row's own body.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"The heading presents the feature as keyboard and theme only, while the body also covers contrast and colour-only status, so the two surfaces describe it differently.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"marketing/styles.css\",\n    \"line\": 720,\n    \"summary\": \"The full-row span rule `:nth-child(3n + 1)` assumes three columns but also fires in the two-column breakpoint; the class name `small-grid-6` no longer matches its seven cards.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"With 4 or 10 cards at 960px wide or narrower, the last card spans a full row while card 3 or 9 sits alone next to an empty cell. That is the orphan the rule exists to prevent. It is correct today only because 7 cards also lands right at two columns.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nComments: https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2521#discussion_r4333504014 (and r4333504136, r4333504253, r4333504365, r4333504531, r4333504660)."}]},"uuid":"12f293f7-6169-4b7f-af99-920968eab09c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:57:23.043Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"commandName":"code-review","status":"forked","agentId":"aeca446f0251f23d6","result":"I reviewed PR #2521 and found six problems, all posted to the PR as inline comments. None is a code bug. Three are claims in the published copy that go further than what CI enforces, two are mismatches between the marketing page and the docs landing page, and one is a layout rule that will misplace cards if the count changes.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"marketing/index.html\",\n    \"line\": 195,\n    \"summary\": \"'status never relies on colour alone' is an absolute claim with no automated check behind it; axe doesn't detect it in general, and no test in rule 4b covers it.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Any chart, trend band, sparkline, tag or calendar cell that shows status by colour only makes the published marketing sentence false.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"marketing/index.html\",\n    \"line\": 195,\n    \"summary\": \"'Every page is checked' overclaims: the axe lanes scan only the app's routes, not the marketing site or the docs site.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A reader on the marketing page reasonably takes 'every page' to include that page and the docs, and neither is scanned. The same wording is on docs/site/index.md:73.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"marketing/index.html\",\n    \"line\": 195,\n    \"summary\": \"CI fails only on axe serious/critical violations (MIN_IMPACT in ratchet.ts), and CONTRIBUTING 4b says the SQL editor, lineage graph and drawer/modal focus return are not covered yet; the unqualified 'accessibility issues' reads as all issues.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A moderate or minor axe violation, or a focus-return bug in a modal, passes CI while the copy implies those pages were checked for it.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"docs/site/index.md\",\n    \"line\": 71,\n    \"summary\": \"The marketing deployment card now names the Helm chart (#2505), but the matching docs landing row was not updated.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Someone reading the docs landing doesn't learn that a Kubernetes/Helm path exists; the two published surfaces disagree.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"docs/site/index.md\",\n    \"line\": 73,\n    \"summary\": \"The docs row heading 'Use it from the keyboard, in either theme' doesn't match the marketing title 'Built with accessibility in mind', and is narrower than the row's own body.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"The heading presents the feature as keyboard and theme only, while the body also covers contrast and colour-only status, so the two surfaces describe it differently.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"marketing/styles.css\",\n    \"line\": 720,\n    \"summary\": \"The full-row span rule `:nth-child(3n + 1)` assumes three columns but also fires in the two-column breakpoint; the class name `small-grid-6` no longer matches its seven cards.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"With 4 or 10 cards at 960px wide or narrower, the last card spans a full row while card 3 or 9 sits alone next to an empty cell. That is the orphan the rule exists to prevent. It is correct today only because 7 cards also lands right at two columns.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nComments: https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2521#discussion_r4333504014 (and r4333504136, r4333504253, r4333504365, r4333504531, r4333504660)."},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b192ec7d-e401-4915-8adc-f93cdbc7d0e1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","root":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"96ef59cd-2be1-4176-aaab-ba93b3406412","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.