{"parentUuid":"405030b5-4418-4c24-a235-fca7189cbf52","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"abc88b6b-0c7f-4068-93a6-b3c2a4b46c76","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013BKF3tUz8ngN79CZW4WA2p","type":"tool_result","content":"| **Run it where the data lives** | Reference deployments on Azure Container Apps and AWS ECS, the recommended way to run DataQ for production and enterprise teams; a single-host Docker stack for evaluation; bring your own identity provider or none at all. |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d6d738ad-bae6-4b87-a680-11d4d90c38bc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:57:40.187Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"| **Run it where the data lives** | Reference deployments on Azure Container Apps and AWS ECS, the recommended way to run DataQ for production and enterprise teams; a single-host Docker stack for evaluation; bring your own identity provider or none at all. |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/docs/site/index.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":70,"oldLines":6,"newStart":70,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | **Alert the right people, once** | Teams, Slack, email and webhooks, routed by severity, de-duplicated so a broken check reports when it breaks, not on every run. |"," | **Run it where the data lives** | Reference deployments on Azure Container Apps and AWS ECS, the recommended way to run DataQ for production and enterprise teams; a single-host Docker stack for evaluation; bring your own identity provider or none at all. |"," | **Let assistants do the work** | Fifty-six MCP tools expose the same actions to Claude, Copilot and Cursor, every one honest about what it cannot see. |","+| **Built with accessibility in mind** | Every screen of the app is scanned for serious accessibility violations in light and dark themes on every change, colour contrast is held to WCAG ratios, severity and run status carry a text label or pattern as well as colour, and core navigation works from the keyboard. A full WCAG conformance review is planned, so this describes the checks, not a conformance claim. |"," "," ## Who it is for"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/marketing/index.html","hunks":[{"oldStart":158,"oldLines":7,"newStart":158,"newLines":7,"lines":["       </div>","     </div>"," ","-    <div class=\"small-grid small-grid-6\">","+    <div class=\"small-grid small-grid-3up\">","       <div class=\"small-card\">","         <span class=\"icon-inline\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3h18v4H3zm0 6h18v4H3zm0 6h18v4H3z\"/></svg></span>","         <div class=\"title\">Assets &amp; lineage</div>"]},{"oldStart":182,"oldLines":13,"newStart":182,"newLines":18,"lines":["       <div class=\"small-card\">","         <span class=\"icon-inline\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 5h18v4H3zm0 5h18v4H3zm0 5h18v4H3z\"/></svg></span>","         <div class=\"title\">Runs where your data lives</div>","-        <div class=\"body\">Reference deployments on Azure Container Apps and AWS ECS, a one-command Docker stack for evaluation, no vendor lock-in behind any seam.</div>","+        <div class=\"body\">Reference stacks for Azure Container Apps and AWS ECS, a Helm chart for your own Kubernetes, a one-command Docker stack for evaluation, no vendor lock-in behind any seam.</div>","       </div>","       <div class=\"small-card\">","         <span class=\"icon-inline\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 6h16v2H4zm0 5h16v2H4zm0 5h10v2H4z\"/></svg></span>","         <div class=\"title\">Documented like a product</div>","         <div class=\"body\">Tutorials with screenshots and clips, a generated reference for every check type, endpoint and tool, forty-plus decision records, and pages your assistant can read as Markdown.</div>","       </div>","+      <div class=\"small-card\">","+        <span class=\"icon-inline\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 2a2 2 0 1 1 0 4 2 2 0 0 1 0-4zm9 7h-6v13h-2v-6h-2v6H9V9H3V7h18z\"/></svg></span>","+        <div class=\"title\">Built with accessibility in mind</div>","+        <div class=\"body\">Every screen of the app is scanned for serious accessibility violations in light and dark themes on every change, colour contrast is held to WCAG ratios, severity and run status carry a text label or pattern as well as colour, and core navigation works from the keyboard.</div>","+      </div>","     </div>","   </div>"," </section>"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/marketing/styles.css","hunks":[{"oldStart":714,"oldLines":9,"newStart":714,"newLines":12,"lines":[" .shots-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: var(--feat-4up-cols); gap: 16px; }"," .shots-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }"," @media (max-width: 720px) { .shots-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }","-.small-grid-6 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }","-@media (max-width: 960px) { .small-grid-6 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }","-@media (max-width: 560px) { .small-grid-6 { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }","+.small-grid-3up { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }","+/* A last card that would sit alone in its row spans the row, at each column count. */","+@media (min-width: 961px) { .small-grid-3up > .small-card:last-child:nth-child(3n + 1) { grid-column: 1 / -1; } }","+@media (min-width: 561px) and (max-width: 960px) { .small-grid-3up > .small-card:last-child:nth-child(2n + 1) { grid-column: 1 / -1; } }","+@media (max-width: 960px) { .small-grid-3up { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }","+@media (max-width: 560px) { .small-grid-3up { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }"," "," /* Demo-profile walkthrough. */"," .walk-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; justify-content: center; margin-top: 24px; }"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/docs/site/index.md","/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/marketing/index.html","/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/marketing/styles.css"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ff28c103-3e0e-4e16-bd7e-81597a6efe86","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","root":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"405030b5-4418-4c24-a235-fca7189cbf52","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main"}
