{"parentUuid":"8f6dfff1-c733-4e20-83e8-c3791e7bb1ec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEsMRxSzHoEocApTzZnT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HEzMPN32zgreJEvQWdMoUR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && B=/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin; for s in scripts/check-docs-*.py; do $B/python $s >/dev/null 2>&1 || echo \"FAIL $s\"; done; $B/python -m mkdocs build --strict -q >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"mkdocs rc=$?\"; git add -A marketing docs/site/index.md && git commit -q -m \"fixup: copy says only what CI checks; span rule per column count; docs row matches\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1 | grep -iE \"failed|error\"; git push -q 2>&1 | grep -iE \"error|rejected\"; gh pr edit 2521 --body \"Maintainer direction (2026-10-21): mention accessibility in the marketing material, worded so it is true today.\n\n- **Marketing page.** A *Built with accessibility in mind* card. It says every screen of the app is scanned for serious accessibility violations in both themes on every change, colour contrast is held to WCAG ratios, severity and run status carry a text label or pattern as well as colour, and core navigation works from the keyboard. Each clause matches a check that exists: rule 4b's axe gate (serious/critical, app routes), \\`tokens.test.ts\\`, the #1671 status components, and \\`keyboard.spec.ts\\`. It makes no WCAG, ADA or EAA conformance claim. That waits for the Week-7 audits (#1672, #1673) and the conformance report filed as #2520.\n- **Docs landing.** A row with the same heading and copy, which says outright it is not a conformance claim. The deployment row now names the Helm chart, as the marketing card does.\n- **Layout.** The grid class is now \\`small-grid-3up\\`. A last card that would sit alone spans its row, using a separate rule at three columns and at two.\n\n**Checked (rule 44).** Headless Chromium at 1280, 900 and 375 px in both themes, with the real 7 cards and with 4. No card is orphaned at any width, there is no horizontal scroll, and axe (WCAG 2 A/AA) finds no violations in the grid in either theme. Docs guards and \\`mkdocs build --strict\\` pass.\n\n- N/A — marketing/docs copy (\\`no-changelog\\`)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" >/dev/null; C=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD); gh api graphql -f query='query{repository(owner:\"TheurgicDuke771\",name:\"DataQ\"){pullRequest(number:2521){reviewThreads(first:20){nodes{id isResolved}}}}}' -q '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[] | select(.isResolved|not) | .id' | while read tid; do gh api graphql -f query='mutation($t:ID!,$b:String!){addPullRequestReviewThreadReply(input:{pullRequestReviewThreadId:$t,body:$b}){comment{id}}}' -f t=$tid -f b=\"Fixed in $C. Card and row copy now: \\\"Every screen of the app is scanned for serious accessibility violations … severity and run status carry a text label or pattern as well as colour …\\\". Each clause maps to an existing check. The docs row uses the same heading and names the Helm chart. The grid class is \\`small-grid-3up\\` and the orphan span has one rule per column count, checked with 7 and 4 cards at 1280, 900 and 375 px.\" >/dev/null && gh api graphql -f query='mutation($t:ID!){resolveReviewThread(input:{threadId:$t}){thread{isResolved}}}' -f t=$tid -q .data.resolveReviewThread.thread.isResolved; done; git checkout -q main","description":"Run guards, commit, update the PR body, resolve the six threads","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1633,"cache_read_input_tokens":708209,"output_tokens":1540,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":61},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral