s.\n- **Layout.** The grid class is now \\`small-grid-3up\\`. A last card that would sit alone spans its row, using a separate rule at three columns and at two.\n\n**Checked (rule 44).** Headless Chromium at 1280, 900 and 375 px in both themes, with the real 7 cards and with 4. No card is orphaned at any width, there is no horizontal scroll, and axe (WCAG 2 A/AA) finds no violations in the grid in either theme. Docs guards and \\`mkdocs build --strict\\` pass.\n\n- N/A — marketing/docs copy (\\`no-changelog\\`)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" >/dev/null; C=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD); gh api graphql -f query='query{repository(owner:\"TheurgicDuke771\",name:\"DataQ\"){pullRequest(number:2521){reviewThreads(first:20){nodes{id isResolved}}}}}' -q '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[] | select(.isResolved|not) | .id' | while read tid; do gh api graphql -f query='mutation($t:ID!,$b:String!){addPullRequestReviewThreadReply(input:{pullRequestReviewThreadId:$t,body:$b}){comment{id}}}' -f t=$tid -f b=\"Fixed in $C. Card and row copy now: \\\"Every screen of the app is scanned for serious accessibility violations … severity and run status carry a text label or pattern as well as colour …\\\". Each clause maps to an existing check. The docs row uses the same heading and names the Helm chart. The grid class is \\`small-grid-3up\\` and the orphan span has one rule per column count, checked with 7 and 4 cards at 1280, 900 and 375 px.\" >/dev/null && gh api graphql -f query='mutation($t:ID!){resolveReviewThread(input:{threadId:$t}){thread{isResolved}}}' -f t=$tid -q .data.resolveReviewThread.thread.isResolved; done; git checkout -q main","description":"Run guards, commit, update the PR body, resolve the six threads","timeout":600000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"591a5509-a196-4422-b89a-32782edab1cd","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgEsMRYeQo8yjSicJnCNw","requestRef":"1b13f8e6-746e-452d-b49f-687f62728b31","requestedModel":"cl